00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.149 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  Sleek design and state-of-the-art  Technology this is one of the most high  profile infrastructure projects in  Indonesia the trains can reach a maximum  speed of 350 kilometers per hour  this week at the close of the G20 Summit  in Bali China's president Xi Jinping  joined the Indonesian president  jokowododo to view a test of the train  we have just witnessed the operational  trial of the Jakarta Bandung high speed  Railway and I'm optimistic about the  operation of the Railway in June next  year this is one of China's many Don  Milton Road initiatives projects that  are part of the country's International  infrastructure development strategy  this is the success that benefits the  people of both countries it also brings  a positive impact to the world as a role  model for cooperation among developing  countries  the trains are also equipped with  sensors to detect earthquakes and other  threats  the railway spans more than 140  kilometers and includes 13 tunnels it  will cut travel time between Jakarta and  bundle from three hours to 40 minutes  it's the first High-Speed Rail Project  outside China that fully incorporates  Chinese technology and Equipment  some of the technology here is being  used for the first time in Indonesia we  are very proud  but the project which is mostly funded  by a loan from the China Development  Bank has been controversial the  Consortium building the railway says the  project faces cost overruns of around 2  billion dollars meaning the estimated  total cost is more than 7 billion  dollars some have criticized the amount  being spent on the project there will be  like many fundamental needs instead of  the  High technological like high-speed  Railway instead of building that kind of  infrastructures that the Indonesian  government should focusing more in the  poverty reductions China is the world's  largest creditor to developing economies  and much of that goes to infrastructure  projects but some say the new train  should be seen as an opportunity not a  liability this is also a chance for  knowledge transfer for Indonesians who  are interested in fast training  technology  Indonesians will have the chance to  assess for themselves how useful the  rail network is when it begins  operations in 2023  Jessica Washington altazira Jakarta

